{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:89083",
  "title": "Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-26 12:00:53"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-27 00:12:50"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: tcp: restrict SO_ATTACH_FILTER to priv users (CVE-2026-53236)\n\n* kernel: fuse: re-lock request before replacing page cache folio (CVE-2026-53388)\n\n* kernel: writeback: fix race between cgroup_writeback_umount() and inode_switch_wbs() (CVE-2026-64378)\n\n* kernel: net: gro: fix double aggregation of flush-marked skbs (CVE-2026-68136)\n\n* kernel: net/packet: avoid fanout hook re-registration after unregister (CVE-2026-68338)\n\n* kernel: net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CVE-2026-68140)\n\n* kernel: net/sched: serialize qdisc_rtab_list against concurrent get/put (CVE-2026-68138)\n\n* kernel: ipvs: reload ip header after head reallocation (CVE-2026-68476)\n\n* kernel: mptcp: options: reset DSS fields in case of unexpected size (CVE-2026-80586)\n\n* kernel: usb: usbfs: fix use-after-free of usb_device in usbdev_release() (CVE-2026-80824)\n\n* kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n\n* kernel: net/iucv: filter frames in afiucv_hs_rcv() by ingress device (CVE-2026-81003)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum\n(CVE-2026-99999)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Backport 6785011f8b16 (\"ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum\") [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-280584)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
